From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 17:18:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 57/62] verimark: drive IT delete 0xA4 over BULK directly (sync
 vtable was CONTROL-only)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause of the 'delete: 0xa4 USB OUT write failed (record 31 B)'
runtime error : verimark_transport_io_bind() only wires the CONTROL
transport (DT path). The IT auto-route to BULK lives exclusively in
the ASYNC transceive path (verimark_transceive_async,
transport.c:492). The sync vtable does NOT route by PID, so binding
it on an IT device makes every OUT send the encrypted record over EP0
control transfers — which the IT firmware refuses, producing the OUT
write error observed.

IT verify / enroll / list / identify work because they all go through
verimark_session_call_opcode_async() → verimark_transceive_async()
→ the BULK auto-route. delete is the only IT-side caller that uses
the SYNC verimark_session_call_opcode() (because delete is fast and
doesn't run in an SSM), so it tripped the missing route.

Fix: in the IT branch of verimark_delete(), drive USB directly via
verimark_bulk_out / verimark_bulk_in on
VERIMARK_IT_EP_BULK_OUT (0x01) / VERIMARK_IT_EP_BULK_IN (0x81),
bypassing the broken sync vtable. The encrypted record (31 B for the
2-byte plaintext [0xA4][sub_factor]) is sent raw over EP01 OUT, and
the encrypted response is read from EP81 IN, then decrypted via
verimark_session_decrypt_appdata as before.

A longer-term cleanup would teach verimark_transport_io_bind() to
PID-route too, but doing it here keeps the change small and
surgical to delete. DT delete is unaffected — it doesn't enter the
IT branch.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 54 +++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index ab9b9cd..a05819f 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -3051,21 +3051,29 @@ static void verimark_delete(FpDevice *device)
             fpi_device_delete_complete(device, g_steal_pointer(&error));
             return;
         }
-        VerimarkTransportIoCtx it_io_ctx = {
-            .h = self->transport,
-            .timeout_ms = 3000,
-        };
-        VerimarkTransportIO it_io;
-        verimark_transport_io_bind(&it_io, &it_io_ctx);
         /* Per RE of fcn.18009a5a0 + doc (it-verify-decode.md § Delete) :
          *   mov edx, 1            ; taille payload = 1
          *   buffer[1] = <byte>    ; sous-facteur ANSI-381
          * → on-wire plaintext = [0xA4][sub_factor] = 2 bytes total.
          *
-         * Inline the call here (instead of verimark_session_call_opcode)
-         * so we can disambiguate the failure step : write vs read vs
-         * decrypt vs short response. The opaque "transport/crypto failure"
-         * black box hid which step was failing at runtime. */
+         * Drive the USB directly via verimark_bulk_out / verimark_bulk_in
+         * on EP01 OUT / EP81 IN, bypassing verimark_transport_io_bind
+         * which is the CONTROL-transport sync vtable (DT path). The
+         * IT auto-route to BULK lives only in the ASYNC transceive path
+         * (verimark_transceive_async, line ~492 of transport.c) ; the
+         * sync vtable does NOT route by PID, so using it on an IT
+         * device makes the firmware refuse the OUT write with the
+         * symptom observed at runtime 2026-06-07 :
+         *
+         *   "delete: 0xa4 USB OUT write failed (record 31 B, ...)"
+         *
+         * The doc IT verify/enroll work because they go through
+         * `_call_opcode_async()` ; delete is sync and used the wrong
+         * vtable.
+         *
+         * On the wire (raw BULK, no framing prefix on AppData) :
+         *   OUT EP01 : [TLS record] (record_len = 5 hdr + 8 nonce + 2 plain + 16 tag = 31 B)
+         *   IN  EP81 : [TLS record] (status + optional payload, decrypted) */
         uint8_t req_record[64];
         size_t req_record_len = verimark_session_encrypt_appdata(
             &self->session, 0xA4, &sub_factor, 1,
@@ -3078,22 +3086,30 @@ static void verimark_delete(FpDevice *device)
             fpi_device_delete_complete(device, g_steal_pointer(&error));
             return;
         }
-        if (!it_io.write(it_io.ctx, req_record, req_record_len,
-                         /*is_handshake*/ false)) {
+        VerimarkResult br = verimark_bulk_out(self->transport,
+                                              VERIMARK_IT_EP_BULK_OUT,
+                                              req_record, req_record_len,
+                                              /*timeout_ms*/ 3000);
+        if (br != VERIMARK_OK) {
             error = g_error_new(FP_DEVICE_ERROR, FP_DEVICE_ERROR_PROTO,
-                                "delete: 0xa4 USB OUT write failed "
-                                "(record %zu B, sub-factor 0x%02x)",
-                                req_record_len, sub_factor);
+                                "delete: 0xa4 BULK OUT EP01 failed "
+                                "(VerimarkResult=%d, record %zu B, sub-factor 0x%02x)",
+                                (int)br, req_record_len, sub_factor);
             fpi_device_delete_complete(device, g_steal_pointer(&error));
             return;
         }
         uint8_t resp_record[4096];
         size_t resp_record_len = 0;
-        if (!it_io.read(it_io.ctx, resp_record, sizeof(resp_record),
-                        &resp_record_len)) {
+        br = verimark_bulk_in(self->transport,
+                              VERIMARK_IT_EP_BULK_IN,
+                              resp_record, sizeof(resp_record),
+                              &resp_record_len,
+                              /*timeout_ms*/ 3000);
+        if (br != VERIMARK_OK) {
             error = g_error_new(FP_DEVICE_ERROR, FP_DEVICE_ERROR_PROTO,
-                                "delete: 0xa4 USB IN read failed/timeout "
-                                "(sub-factor 0x%02x)", sub_factor);
+                                "delete: 0xa4 BULK IN EP81 failed/timeout "
+                                "(VerimarkResult=%d, sub-factor 0x%02x)",
+                                (int)br, sub_factor);
             fpi_device_delete_complete(device, g_steal_pointer(&error));
             return;
         }
